{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792865670,"nonce":"5t4ovz+tHIqo3f/jWzNUBe08K58=","title":"A static method is not reachable through a class used as a value","message":"`haxe_dynamic_field` on a class token looks the name up in STATIC_FIELDS, which only holds getter/setter thunks for static variables. A static method is never registered, so the lookup returns null and the call site's fallback runs instead: for `t.f(1)` with `t:Dynamic = C`, that fallback calls `C.f` with a receiver it does not take (an over-arity call; Cranelift traps it, the interpreter refuses it).\n\nReproducer (native start, any opt level that does not inline `tfd`):\n\n    class C { public static function f(i:Int) { return \"f\" + i; } }\n    class Main {\n      static function tfd(t:Dynamic) { return t.f(1); }\n      static function main() { trace(tfd(C)); }\n    }\n\nprints `\u003cunknown type …\u003e` instead of `f1`. Conformance Issue4910 passes only because O0 inlining folds `tfd(C)` into a static call.\n\nFix direction: register each static method of a class that is used as a value (e.g. alongside haxe_register_static_field in `__vtable_init__`) and have type_value_field return it as a closure; drop the receiver-passing fallback for class tokens.","files":null}]}